      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8357793::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC6728353::web::017::atomistic_modeling_of_hea_nanoparticles"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "HEA nanoparticle populations can be prepared with nearly identical composition and size while differing principally in their degree of SRO.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid thermal quenching can preserve a nearly random chemical state, whereas prolonged post-synthesis annealing can enhance SRO.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11265590::web::024::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Composition, particle size, and external environment should be held constant when testing the effect of SRO.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chemical SRO changes the local atomic-bonding environment.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11265590::web::024::conclusions",
        "PMC6728353::web::017::atomistic_modeling_of_hea_nanoparticles"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chemical SRO pins defects at the nanoparticle surface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8357793::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC6728353::web::017::atomistic_modeling_of_hea_nanoparticles"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A more defined SRO-derived local arrangement creates stronger interatomic bonding and additional defect obstacles.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11265590::web::024::conclusions",
        "PMC8357793::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The bonding and defect obstacles produced by SRO raise the energy barrier for surface-atom migration.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Raising the barrier for surface-atom migration delays the onset of surface premelting.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SRO-enhanced nanoparticles will have a measurably higher premelting-onset temperature than randomly ordered counterparts.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "SRO-enhanced nanoparticles will have a measurably higher overall melting temperature than randomly ordered counterparts.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed relationship should hold for HEA nanoparticles of similar size and composition in regimes where surface effects are significant.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6728353::web::017::atomistic_modeling_of_hea_nanoparticles"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relationship may fail at extreme particle sizes or in compositions with strong phase segregation that overrides SRO effects.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnitude of the melting-temperature shift depends on composition, nanoparticle size, and processing parameters.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to observe a statistically significant increase in either premelting onset or melting temperature, or observation of a decrease, would falsify the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
